(ns stevetrading.execution.core
  "Execution planning stage (STRATEGY_PIPELINE §5.6, ARCHITECTURE §19).

  Pure pipeline component: expresses a risk-approved signal as a canonical
  execution plan plus order intents. Order intents are FULL
  :fact/order-intent-created payloads (CANONICAL_SCHEMAS §11.3) whose ids
  come from the deterministic order-intent identity algorithm
  (domain.schemas/order-intent-id, §12) — replay-stable, never random.
  Legs are ALWAYS stored canonically sorted (§12.3) regardless of
  declaration order, and the identity algorithm canonicalizes legs
  independently, so the same leg SET always yields the same intent id.

  v0.1 policy :execution/market-equity-v1: single-leg equity market order,
  :tif/day, quantity from the risk stage.
  - :posture/enter-long -> buy/open, role :intent-role/entry
  - :posture/flatten    -> sell/close, role :intent-role/exit
  - approved quantity of zero (e.g. flatten with no open position) plans
    NO intents (empty :execution/order-intents)

  Phase 9 multi-leg policies (instrument-ctx carries the leg
  configuration; the risk-approved signal carries :decision/net-credit —
  the current spread mid from the chain feature — used as the net
  credit/debit limit price):

  :execution/vertical-credit-spread-v1 — TWO legs in ONE intent:
  sell the near strike, buy the far strike (same expiry, same right).
  instrument-ctx :execution/spread is a
  domain.instruments/vertical-spread-context map.
  - :posture/enter-long -> entry: intent side :order-side/sell (net
    credit), effect :position-effect/open, limit order at the net-credit
    mid, legs [near SELL, far BUY]
  - :posture/flatten -> exit: intent side :order-side/buy (net debit),
    effect :position-effect/close, limit at the current mid, legs
    mirrored [near BUY, far SELL]

  :execution/iron-condor-v1 — FOUR legs in ONE intent: a put credit
  spread + a call credit spread. instrument-ctx :execution/condor is
  {:condor/put-spread <vertical-spread-context> :condor/call-spread
  <vertical-spread-context>}.
  - :posture/enter-long -> entry: sell both near strikes, buy both far
    strikes; side sell/open, net-credit limit
  - :posture/flatten -> exit: all four legs mirrored; side buy/close

  Position-effect convention for spreads (documented; consumed by the
  ledger derivation): the ENTRY intent uses :position-effect/open with
  per-leg sides — the sell legs open SHORT lots, the buy legs open LONG
  lots. The EXIT intent uses :position-effect/close with mirrored per-leg
  sides, closing both lot kinds. The per-leg side travels on the legs
  themselves; ledger.core resolves each fill's side from the intent leg
  matching the fill's instrument.

  Steve-v2 bridge direction policies (instrument-ctx additionally carries
  :execution/strategy-view — the strategy's :portfolio/by-strategy
  sub-view; the option policy also reads :execution/chain — the market
  slice's latest :fact/option-chain-observed payload — and
  :execution/spot — the last bar close decimal string):

  :execution/equity-direction-v1 — single-leg SPY market orders,
  :tif/day. The executor receives ONE posture; a FLIP (entering while an
  OPPOSITE net position exists in the strategy view) emits TWO intents in
  one plan: slot 0 closes the existing net position, slot 1 opens the new
  one. Entry quantity = :risk/approved-quantity; close quantity = |net|
  from the view (never the risk quantity).
  - :posture/enter-long  -> buy/open (after sell-close of any short)
  - :posture/enter-short -> sell/open, opens a SHORT lot (after
    sell-close of any long)
  - :posture/flatten     -> close the net position (side opposite the net
    sign, qty |net|); no position -> NO intents

  :execution/single-leg-option-atm-v1 — long single options as direction
  proxy (OAK/DOLPHIN). ATM = the chain contract of the wanted right with
  BOTH quotes whose strike is closest to spot (ties -> lower strike);
  entries are LIMIT at the (bid+ask)/2 mid rounded to 2dp.
  - :posture/enter-long  -> BUY the ATM CALL (limit at mid)
  - :posture/enter-short -> BUY the ATM PUT (limit at mid)
  - :posture/flatten     -> one close intent per open option lot in the
    strategy view (FIFO slot order): side opposite the lot side, limit at
    the contract's current mid, or a MARKET order when the contract is no
    longer quoted two-sided in the chain
  - flip -> close every open option lot (slots 0..n-1) + open the new
    contract (slot n) in one plan
  - NO chain in the slice -> NO intents; plan-execution returns
    :execution/skip-reason :skip/no-chain (the pipeline then emits no
    plan/intent facts). Likewise :skip/no-spot (no bars yet) and
    :skip/no-eligible-contract (chain present but no two-sided contract
    of the wanted right)."
  (:require [stevetrading.domain.instruments :as instruments]
            [stevetrading.domain.schemas :as schemas])
  (:import decimal))

(defn- order-intent
  "Build one full :fact/order-intent-created payload (§11.3) with its
  deterministic id (§12.1 identity input). Accepts EITHER :legs (explicit
  multi-leg vector) or :instrument-id (single-leg convenience, leg side =
  intent side). Legs are canonically sorted (§12.3) before identity
  hashing and payload storage."
  [{:keys [decision-id intent-slot role side effect order-type tif
           quantity instrument-id legs limit-price account-id]}]
  (let [legs (instruments/canonical-leg-sort
              (or legs
                  [{:instrument/id instrument-id
                    :leg/side side
                    :leg/quantity quantity}]))
        intent-id (schemas/order-intent-id
                   {:identity/version 1
                    :identity/decision-id decision-id
                    :identity/intent-slot intent-slot
                    :identity/account-id account-id
                    :identity/role role
                    :identity/order-shape {:side side
                                           :effect effect
                                           :order-type order-type
                                           :time-in-force tif
                                           :quantity quantity
                                           :limit-price limit-price
                                           :stop-price nil
                                           :legs legs}})]
    {:order-intent/id intent-id
     :order-intent/decision-id decision-id
     :order-intent/intent-slot intent-slot
     :order-intent/account-id account-id
     :order-intent/role role
     :order-intent/side side
     :order-intent/effect effect
     :order-intent/order-type order-type
     :order-intent/time-in-force tif
     :order-intent/quantity quantity
     :order-intent/limit-price limit-price
     :order-intent/stop-price nil
     :order-intent/legs legs}))

(defn- zero-qty?
  [quantity]
  (zero? (decimal/Decimal (or quantity "0"))))

(defn- unplannable-posture!
  [policy posture]
  (throw (ex-info (str "no " policy " expression for posture "
                       (pr-str posture))
                  {:error/code :error/unplannable-posture
                   :error/policy policy
                   :error/posture posture})))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/market-equity-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- market-equity-v1
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
        posture (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        instrument-id (:instrument/id instrument-ctx)]
    (if (zero-qty? quantity)
      []
      (case posture
        :posture/enter-long
        [(order-intent {:decision-id decision-id
                        :intent-slot 0
                        :role :intent-role/entry
                        :side :order-side/buy
                        :effect :position-effect/open
                        :order-type :order-type/market
                        :tif :tif/day
                        :quantity quantity
                        :limit-price nil
                        :instrument-id instrument-id
                        :account-id account-id})]

        :posture/flatten
        [(order-intent {:decision-id decision-id
                        :intent-slot 0
                        :role :intent-role/exit
                        :side :order-side/sell
                        :effect :position-effect/close
                        :order-type :order-type/market
                        :tif :tif/day
                        :quantity quantity
                        :limit-price nil
                        :instrument-id instrument-id
                        :account-id account-id})]

        (unplannable-posture! :execution/market-equity-v1 posture)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Multi-leg helpers
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- spread-legs
  "Entry legs for one vertical credit spread: sell near, buy far.
  exit? mirrors both sides (buy near, sell far)."
  [spread-ctx quantity exit?]
  [{:instrument/id (:spread/near-instrument-id spread-ctx)
    :leg/side (if exit? :order-side/buy :order-side/sell)
    :leg/quantity quantity}
   {:instrument/id (:spread/far-instrument-id spread-ctx)
    :leg/side (if exit? :order-side/sell :order-side/buy)
    :leg/quantity quantity}])

(defn- require-ctx
  [instrument-ctx k policy]
  (or (get instrument-ctx k)
      (throw (ex-info (str policy " requires " k " in instrument-ctx")
                      {:error/code :error/missing-execution-context
                       :error/policy policy
                       :error/key k}))))

(defn- multi-leg-intent
  [{:keys [risk-approved-signal account-id legs policy]}]
  (let [posture (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal)
        base {:decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
              :intent-slot 0
              :order-type :order-type/limit
              :tif :tif/day
              :quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
              :limit-price (:decision/net-credit risk-approved-signal)
              :legs legs
              :account-id account-id}]
    (case posture
      :posture/enter-long
      [(order-intent (assoc base
                            :role :intent-role/entry
                            :side :order-side/sell
                            :effect :position-effect/open))]

      :posture/flatten
      [(order-intent (assoc base
                            :role :intent-role/exit
                            :side :order-side/buy
                            :effect :position-effect/close))]

      (unplannable-posture! policy posture))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/vertical-credit-spread-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- vertical-credit-spread-v1
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [spread (require-ctx instrument-ctx :execution/spread
                            :execution/vertical-credit-spread-v1)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        exit? (= :posture/flatten (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal))]
    (if (zero-qty? quantity)
      []
      (multi-leg-intent {:risk-approved-signal risk-approved-signal
                         :account-id account-id
                         :legs (spread-legs spread quantity exit?)
                         :policy :execution/vertical-credit-spread-v1}))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/iron-condor-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- iron-condor-v1
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [condor (require-ctx instrument-ctx :execution/condor
                            :execution/iron-condor-v1)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        exit? (= :posture/flatten (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal))]
    (if (zero-qty? quantity)
      []
      (multi-leg-intent {:risk-approved-signal risk-approved-signal
                         :account-id account-id
                         :legs (into (spread-legs (:condor/put-spread condor)
                                                  quantity exit?)
                                     (spread-legs (:condor/call-spread condor)
                                                  quantity exit?))
                         :policy :execution/iron-condor-v1}))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/equity-direction-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- view-net
  "Net position Decimal for instrument-id in a :portfolio/by-strategy
  sub-view (nil view -> 0)."
  [strategy-view instrument-id]
  (decimal/Decimal
   (or (get-in strategy-view [:view/net-positions instrument-id]) "0")))

(defn- equity-direction-v1
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
        posture (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        instrument-id (:instrument/id instrument-ctx)
        net (view-net (:execution/strategy-view instrument-ctx) instrument-id)
        base {:decision-id decision-id
              :order-type :order-type/market
              :tif :tif/day
              :limit-price nil
              :instrument-id instrument-id
              :account-id account-id}
        close-intent (fn [slot]
                       (order-intent
                        (assoc base
                               :intent-slot slot
                               :role :intent-role/exit
                               :side (if (pos? net)
                                       :order-side/sell
                                       :order-side/buy)
                               :effect :position-effect/close
                               :quantity (str (abs net)))))
        open-intent (fn [slot side]
                      (order-intent
                       (assoc base
                              :intent-slot slot
                              :role :intent-role/entry
                              :side side
                              :effect :position-effect/open
                              :quantity quantity)))
        ;; flip = close the opposite net position (slot 0) then open
        ;; (slot 1); same-direction entry is risk-denied upstream — plan
        ;; nothing rather than double up if it ever reaches here.
        enter (fn [side opposite?]
                (cond
                  (zero-qty? quantity) []
                  (zero? net) [(open-intent 0 side)]
                  opposite? [(close-intent 0) (open-intent 1 side)]
                  :else []))]
    (case posture
      :posture/enter-long  (enter :order-side/buy (neg? net))
      ;; :allow-short? false (declaration execution :params — the six-bot
      ;; Alpaca paper accounts reject short opens with 403 forbidden,
      ;; observed live 2026-06-11): a :short posture degrades to
      ;; flatten-only — close any long, never open a short lot.
      :posture/enter-short
      (if (false? (get-in instrument-ctx [:execution/params :allow-short?]))
        (if (pos? net) [(close-intent 0)] [])
        (enter :order-side/sell (pos? net)))
      :posture/flatten     (if (zero? net) [] [(close-intent 0)])
      (unplannable-posture! :execution/equity-direction-v1 posture))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/single-leg-option-atm-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(def ^:private dec-two (decimal/Decimal "2"))
(def ^:private dec-cent (decimal/Decimal "0.01"))

(defn- contract-mid
  "Two-sided (bid+ask)/2 mid Decimal for one chain contract, or nil."
  [contract]
  (let [bid (:quote/bid contract)
        ask (:quote/ask contract)]
    (when (and (some? bid) (some? ask))
      (/ (+ (decimal/Decimal bid) (decimal/Decimal ask)) dec-two))))

(defn- mid-2dp
  "Limit-price decimal string: mid rounded to 2dp (Decimal quantize,
  default half-even)."
  [mid]
  (str (.quantize mid dec-cent)))

(defn- atm-contract
  "The chain contract of the wanted right (:option-right/call|put) with
  both quotes whose strike is closest to spot. Deterministic ties: lower
  strike. Returns {:instrument/id .. :mid Decimal} or nil."
  [chain spot right]
  (->> (:chain/contracts chain)
       (keep (fn [c]
               (let [ref (instruments/parse-instrument-id (:instrument/id c))
                     mid (contract-mid c)]
                 (when (and (some? mid)
                            (= :asset-class/option
                               (:instrument/asset-class ref))
                            (= right (:instrument/right ref)))
                   {:instrument/id (:instrument/id c)
                    :mid mid
                    :strike (decimal/Decimal (:instrument/strike ref))}))))
       (sort-by (fn [{:keys [strike]}]
                  (python/tuple [(abs (- strike spot)) strike])))
       (first)))

(defn- chain-mids
  "{instrument-id mid-Decimal} for every two-sided contract in the chain."
  [chain]
  (into {}
        (keep (fn [c]
                (when-let [mid (contract-mid c)]
                  [(:instrument/id c) mid])))
        (:chain/contracts chain)))

(defn- chain-pxs
  "{instrument-id {:bid Decimal :ask Decimal}} for every two-sided
  contract in the chain (marketable-limit pricing inputs)."
  [chain]
  (into {}
        (keep (fn [c]
                (let [bid (:quote/bid c)
                      ask (:quote/ask c)]
                  (when (and (some? bid) (some? ask))
                    [(:instrument/id c)
                     {:bid (decimal/Decimal bid)
                      :ask (decimal/Decimal ask)}]))))
        (:chain/contracts chain)))

(defn- open-option-lots
  [strategy-view]
  (filterv #(.startswith (str (:lot/instrument-id %)) "option/")
           (:view/open-lots strategy-view)))

(defn- close-option-lot-intents
  "One close intent per open option lot, FIFO slot order. Side opposite
  the lot side. MARKETABLE limit (2026-06-11 fix — mid-priced limits
  rested unfilled across signal flips and the book accumulated outside
  the engine's model): selling a long lot prices at the BID, buying back
  a short lot prices at the ASK; market order when the contract is no
  longer quoted two-sided."
  [{:keys [decision-id account-id lots pxs]}]
  (vec
   (map-indexed
    (fn [slot lot]
      (let [iid (:lot/instrument-id lot)
            px (get pxs iid)
            closing-side (if (= :order-side/sell (:lot/side lot))
                           :order-side/buy
                           :order-side/sell)
            limit (when px
                    (if (= :order-side/buy closing-side)
                      (:ask px)
                      (:bid px)))]
        (order-intent {:decision-id decision-id
                       :intent-slot slot
                       :role :intent-role/exit
                       :side closing-side
                       :effect :position-effect/close
                       :order-type (if limit
                                     :order-type/limit
                                     :order-type/market)
                       :tif :tif/day
                       :quantity (:lot/remaining-quantity lot)
                       :limit-price (when limit (mid-2dp limit))
                       :instrument-id iid
                       :account-id account-id})))
    lots)))

(defn- skip
  [reason]
  {:execution/order-intents []
   :execution/skip-reason reason})

(defn- single-leg-option-atm-v1
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
        posture (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        chain (:execution/chain instrument-ctx)
        spot-str (:execution/spot instrument-ctx)
        lots (open-option-lots (:execution/strategy-view instrument-ctx))
        pxs (chain-pxs chain)
        closes (fn [] (close-option-lot-intents
                       {:decision-id decision-id
                        :account-id account-id
                        :lots lots
                        :pxs pxs}))
        enter (fn [right]
                (cond
                  (zero-qty? quantity) []
                  (nil? spot-str) (skip :skip/no-spot)
                  :else
                  (let [pick (atm-contract chain
                                           (decimal/Decimal spot-str)
                                           right)]
                    (if (nil? pick)
                      (skip :skip/no-eligible-contract)
                      ;; flip: close every open option lot first (only
                      ;; opposite-direction lots can exist — same-direction
                      ;; entries are risk-denied), then open. Entry buys
                      ;; price at the ASK (marketable limit — see
                      ;; close-option-lot-intents docstring).
                      (let [close-intents (closes)
                            ask (get-in pxs [(:instrument/id pick) :ask])]
                        (conj close-intents
                              (order-intent
                               {:decision-id decision-id
                                :intent-slot (count close-intents)
                                :role :intent-role/entry
                                :side :order-side/buy
                                :effect :position-effect/open
                                :order-type :order-type/limit
                                :tif :tif/day
                                :quantity quantity
                                :limit-price (mid-2dp (or ask (:mid pick)))
                                :instrument-id (:instrument/id pick)
                                :account-id account-id})))))))]
    (if (nil? chain)
      (skip :skip/no-chain)
      (case posture
        :posture/enter-long  (enter :option-right/call)
        :posture/enter-short (enter :option-right/put)
        :posture/flatten     (closes)
        (unplannable-posture! :execution/single-leg-option-atm-v1
                              posture)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; :execution/calendar-spread-v1
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(def ^:private dec-floor (decimal/Decimal "0.01"))

(defn- contracts-by-expiry
  "{expiry {strike-Decimal {:instrument/id ..}}} for two-sided contracts
  of the wanted right in a (multi-expiration merged) chain."
  [chain right]
  (reduce
   (fn [acc c]
     (let [ref (instruments/parse-instrument-id (:instrument/id c))]
       (if (and (some? (contract-mid c))
                (= :asset-class/option (:instrument/asset-class ref))
                (= right (:instrument/right ref)))
         (assoc-in acc
                   [(:instrument/expiry ref)
                    (decimal/Decimal (:instrument/strike ref))]
                   {:instrument/id (:instrument/id c)})
         acc)))
   {}
   (:chain/contracts chain)))

(defn- calendar-pair
  "ATM front/back contract pair for a calendar spread: front = earliest
  expiry in the chain, back = next; strike = closest to spot quoted
  two-sided in BOTH expiries (ties -> lower strike). Returns
  {:front-id .. :back-id ..} or nil."
  [chain spot right]
  (let [by-exp (contracts-by-expiry chain right)
        exps (sort (keys by-exp))]
    (when (>= (count exps) 2)
      (let [[front-exp back-exp] exps
            front (get by-exp front-exp)
            back (get by-exp back-exp)
            strike (->> (keys front)
                        (filter #(contains? back %))
                        (sort-by (fn [s] (python/tuple [(abs (- s spot)) s])))
                        first)]
        (when strike
          {:front-id (get-in front [strike :instrument/id])
           :back-id (get-in back [strike :instrument/id])})))))

(defn- net-leg-limit
  "Marketable net limit for a set of priced legs: buys pay the ASK,
  sells receive the BID. Positive net = debit (intent side BUY);
  negative = credit (intent side SELL). Returns
  {:side .. :limit \"x.xx\"} or nil when any leg is unquoted (caller
  falls back to a market order)."
  [legs pxs]
  (let [vals (map (fn [leg]
                    (when-let [px (get pxs (:instrument/id leg))]
                      (if (= :order-side/buy (:leg/side leg))
                        (:ask px)
                        (- (:bid px)))))
                  legs)]
    (when (every? some? vals)
      (let [net (reduce + (decimal/Decimal "0") vals)]
        (if (neg? net)
          {:side :order-side/sell :limit (mid-2dp (max (- net) dec-floor))}
          {:side :order-side/buy :limit (mid-2dp (max net dec-floor))})))))

(defn- calendar-spread-v1
  "TWO legs, SAME strike + right, DIFFERENT expirations, in ONE intent.
  Long calendar (:posture/enter-long — slope widening): SELL the front
  expiry, BUY the back; net debit, marketable limit (back ask - front
  bid). Short calendar (:posture/enter-short): mirrored; net credit;
  gated by :allow-short? (default TRUE — sim strategies). Flatten: one
  multi-leg intent mirroring every open option lot in the strategy view
  (market order when any leg is no longer quoted two-sided). Skips:
  :skip/no-chain, :skip/no-spot, :skip/no-eligible-contract (no strike
  two-sided in BOTH expiries)."
  [risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
        posture (:decision/posture risk-approved-signal)
        quantity (:risk/approved-quantity risk-approved-signal)
        chain (:execution/chain instrument-ctx)
        spot-str (:execution/spot instrument-ctx)
        params (:execution/params instrument-ctx)
        right (or (:right params) :option-right/call)
        lots (open-option-lots (:execution/strategy-view instrument-ctx))
        pxs (chain-pxs chain)
        intent (fn [{:keys [role effect legs slot]}]
                 (let [priced (net-leg-limit legs pxs)]
                   (order-intent {:decision-id decision-id
                                  :intent-slot (or slot 0)
                                  :role role
                                  :side (or (:side priced) :order-side/buy)
                                  :effect effect
                                  :order-type (if priced
                                                :order-type/limit
                                                :order-type/market)
                                  :tif :tif/day
                                  :quantity quantity
                                  :limit-price (:limit priced)
                                  :legs legs
                                  :account-id account-id})))
        close-legs (when (seq lots)
                     (mapv (fn [lot]
                             {:instrument/id (:lot/instrument-id lot)
                              :leg/side (if (= :order-side/sell (:lot/side lot))
                                          :order-side/buy
                                          :order-side/sell)
                              :leg/quantity (:lot/remaining-quantity lot)})
                           lots))
        closes (fn []
                 (if close-legs
                   [(intent {:role :intent-role/exit
                             :effect :position-effect/close
                             :legs close-legs})]
                   []))
        enter (fn [front-side back-side]
                (cond
                  (zero-qty? quantity) []
                  (nil? spot-str) (skip :skip/no-spot)
                  :else
                  (let [pair (calendar-pair chain (decimal/Decimal spot-str)
                                            right)]
                    (if (nil? pair)
                      (skip :skip/no-eligible-contract)
                      ;; flip: close any open structure first, then open
                      (let [close-intents (closes)]
                        (conj close-intents
                              (intent {:role :intent-role/entry
                                       :effect :position-effect/open
                                       :slot (count close-intents)
                                       :legs [{:instrument/id (:front-id pair)
                                               :leg/side front-side
                                               :leg/quantity quantity}
                                              {:instrument/id (:back-id pair)
                                               :leg/side back-side
                                               :leg/quantity quantity}]})))))))]
    (if (nil? chain)
      (skip :skip/no-chain)
      (case posture
        ;; long calendar: sell front, buy back
        :posture/enter-long (enter :order-side/sell :order-side/buy)
        ;; short (reverse) calendar: buy front, sell back
        :posture/enter-short
        (if (false? (:allow-short? params))
          (closes)
          (enter :order-side/buy :order-side/sell))
        :posture/flatten (closes)
        (unplannable-posture! :execution/calendar-spread-v1 posture)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; plan-execution
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn plan-execution
  "Plan order expression for a risk-approved signal under an execution
  policy. risk-approved-signal is the signal decision map merged with the
  risk result (needs :decision/id, :decision/posture,
  :risk/approved-quantity; multi-leg policies also read
  :decision/net-credit). instrument-ctx is {:instrument/id ..} plus the
  policy's leg configuration (:execution/spread or :execution/condor).

  Returns {:execution/plan {:execution/policy-id ..
                            :execution/decision-id ..
                            :execution/order-intent-ids [..]}
           :execution/order-intents [full §11.3 payloads]}
  plus :execution/skip-reason when a policy planned nothing for a stated
  reason (e.g. :skip/no-chain — see ns docstring).

  Deterministic; throws ex-info on unknown policy ids."
  [policy risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id]
  (let [result (case policy
                 :execution/market-equity-v1
                 (market-equity-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 :execution/vertical-credit-spread-v1
                 (vertical-credit-spread-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 :execution/iron-condor-v1
                 (iron-condor-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 :execution/equity-direction-v1
                 (equity-direction-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 :execution/single-leg-option-atm-v1
                 (single-leg-option-atm-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 :execution/calendar-spread-v1
                 (calendar-spread-v1 risk-approved-signal instrument-ctx account-id)
                 (throw (ex-info (str "unknown execution policy: " (pr-str policy))
                                 {:error/code :error/unknown-execution-policy
                                  :error/policy policy})))
        ;; policies return a vector of intents, or a {:execution/order-intents
        ;; [] :execution/skip-reason ..} map when skipping for a reason
        intents (if (map? result) (:execution/order-intents result) result)
        skip-reason (when (map? result) (:execution/skip-reason result))]
    (cond-> {:execution/plan {:execution/policy-id policy
                              :execution/decision-id (:decision/id risk-approved-signal)
                              :execution/order-intent-ids (mapv :order-intent/id intents)}
             :execution/order-intents intents}
      (some? skip-reason) (assoc :execution/skip-reason skip-reason))))
